data.content:
It works. Here's the full `Program.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Jane", 30);
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase });
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` passed via `JsonSerializerOptions` — it converts `Name` → `name` and `Age` → `age`. The record declaration goes after the top-level statements (a C# requirement).
